{"chapter": "defos", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "08S3", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$A \\to B$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{smoothing-proposition-lift-smooth}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:98e96aab4a499c5ef44a83e1b263bd055c8643aea9540d70a4eab383cbc79da2", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:42320cc0f67e1f1d2d03bffa04d47cd61be1a6901c1c2a7cc9814706bd099c8b", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIf our ring map <MATH_0001> is a local complete intersection, then there\nis a solution. This is a kind of lifting result; observe that\nfor syntomic ring maps we have proved a rather strong lifting result in\nSmoothing Ring Maps, Proposition <REF_0001>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:1af547484dcc7cb327e97e9386dd355adc12a7cd111d7327680aeceb1ea72877", "unit_id": "tag:08S3:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "defos", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "08S3", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$A \\to B$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{equation-to-solve}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-existence-lci}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:98e96aab4a499c5ef44a83e1b263bd055c8643aea9540d70a4eab383cbc79da2", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a0d15ea1ea9429c2632f29c5c4f2b2c7fb68bc2031641e16237a97147b729efe", "source_text": "If <MATH_0001> is a local complete intersection ring map, then\nthere exists a solution to (<REF_0001>).\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:53ffad2deaa4c7e5d276aed635f55bbc0111db0842d7ca3d09911da72a754486", "unit_id": "tag:08S6:statement"}
{"chapter": "defos", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "08S3", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$B = A[x_1, \\ldots, x_n]/J$", "MATH_0002": "$J$", "MATH_0003": "$J$", "MATH_0004": "$H_1$", "MATH_0005": "$J' \\subset A'[x_1, \\ldots, x_n]$", "MATH_0006": "$J$", "MATH_0007": "$I[x_1, \\ldots, x_n]$", "MATH_0008": "$A'[x_1, \\ldots, x_n] \\to A[x_1, \\ldots, x_n]$", "MATH_0009": "$I[x_1, \\ldots, x_n] \\cap (J')^2 = J'I[x_1, \\ldots, x_n] =\nJI[x_1, \\ldots, x_n]$", "MATH_0010": "$$\n0 \\to I \\otimes_A B \\to J'/(J')^2 \\to J/J^2 \\to 0\n$$", "MATH_0011": "$J/J^2$", "MATH_0012": "$$\nJ'/(J')^2 = I \\otimes_A B \\oplus J/J^2 \n$$", "MATH_0013": "$(J')^2 \\subset J'' \\subset J'$", "MATH_0014": "$$\n0 \\to I \\otimes_A B \\to A'[x_1, \\ldots, x_n]/J'' \\to B \\to 0\n$$", "MATH_0015": "$N = I \\otimes_A B$", "MATH_0016": "$I \\otimes_A B \\to N$", "PROOFARGEND_0001": "]\n", "REF_0001": "\\ref{more-algebra-definition-local-complete-intersection}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{more-algebra-section-ideals}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{more-algebra-lemma-conormal-sequence-H1-regular-ideal}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{more-algebra-lemma-quasi-regular-ideal-finite-projective}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{equation-to-solve}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}[", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:54cfd3e1b03fc056df225b99919bdff76f915e1b3dd5800f756d9cf28e7572ee", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:001eae63131a435cdedc215729ec5898c87f0402df624bf137af4d8d53dc8bdf", "source_text": "First proof<PROOFARGEND_0001>Write <MATH_0001>. By More on Algebra, Definition\n<REF_0001>\nthe ideal <MATH_0002> is Koszul-regular. This implies <MATH_0003> is <MATH_0004>-regular and\nquasi-regular, see More on Algebra, Section <REF_0002>.\nLet <MATH_0005>\nbe the inverse image of <MATH_0006>. Denote <MATH_0007> the\nkernel of <MATH_0008>.\nBy More on Algebra, Lemma\n<REF_0003> we have\n<MATH_0009>. Hence we obtain a short exact sequence\n<MATH_0010>\nSince <MATH_0011> is projective (More on Algebra, Lemma\n<REF_0004>)\nwe can choose a splitting of this sequence\n<MATH_0012>\nLet <MATH_0013> be the elements which map to the\nsecond summand in the decomposition above. Then\n<MATH_0014>\nis a solution to (<REF_0005>) with <MATH_0015>.\nThe general case is obtained by doing a pushout along the given\nmap <MATH_0016>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a0e23b696b01bc9baf71e9aad3551e2bdaf7054f7e2c06e255858c3e72208dfb", "unit_id": "tag:08S6:proof"}
{"chapter": "defos", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "08S3", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\NL_{A/A'} \\otimes_A B \\to \\NL_{B/A'} \\to \\NL_{B/A}$", "MATH_0002": "$D(B)$", "MATH_0003": "$\\Ext^2_B(\\NL_{B/A}, N)$", "MATH_0004": "$\\NL_{B/A}$", "MATH_0005": "$[-1, 0]$", "MATH_0006": "$\\Ext^2$", "PROOFARGEND_0001": "]\n", "REF_0001": "\\ref{remark-parametrize-solutions}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{more-algebra-lemma-transitive-lci-at-end}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{more-algebra-lemma-lci-NL}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{more-algebra-lemma-splitting-unique}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}[", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:2d0b0d5acb159b259c567d4769c4815347f21a94f6971c42a48e08d4b3f4ef64", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:1c40c9a308b0480ed68ff67ea6531512785801b4cdb8c898852a1b94eb2723db", "source_text": "Second proof<PROOFARGEND_0001>Please read Remark <REF_0001>\nbefore reading this proof. By\nMore on Algebra, Lemma <REF_0002>\nthe maps <MATH_0001>\ndo form a distinguished triangle in <MATH_0002>.\nHence it suffices to show that <MATH_0003> vanishes.\nBy More on Algebra, Lemma <REF_0003>\nthe complex <MATH_0004> is perfect of tor-amplitude in\n<MATH_0005>. This implies our <MATH_0006> vanishes for example\nby More on Algebra, Lemma <REF_0004> part (1).\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f9fda3280f6fadd3b55d00456258b302d5dbc72bfb4a8daf4d256fa7150e2211", "unit_id": "tag:08S6:proof-002"}
